{
 "_comment": "Nexus feature map: every GET page/API -> the sources it shows -> how fresh each must be. Read by nexus_verify.py (PASS/STALE/DEAD/DRIFT) and by the steward. A new GET route must land here (pages) or in excluded, or nexus_verify reports DRIFT. Source kinds: agenda_board (agenda {p:id} lines vs board status), connector (nexus_contract.envelope(name): DEAD on error/source_missing, STALE on a warning or an old as_of - preferred for anything nexus_sources serves), fleet_check (reuse a fleet.py check, no duplicate logic), file_age, glob_newest, sqlite_max (SQL returns one UTC timestamp), json_field (file + dotted key holding an ISO timestamp), dir_present, nonempty (module:function must return something non-empty - catches 'empty = all clear'), user_store (Aern-entered data: no freshness, page must render). stale_after_h null = no freshness bar. fallback: true = the page uses this source only when its primary is empty; it is probed and reported but does not set the page verdict. cf_expect: a Cloudflare-shaped request must get 404 (default) or, with \"decoy\", a 200 whose tiny body differs from the internal one (/api/restock answers {status: ok} with no data). post_guards: write endpoints that must 404 to a Cloudflare-shaped POST (probed with an empty body, so a missing gate gets a 400 and never a write).",
 "version": 2,
